+---
+id: task-003-review-applypatch-conformance-to-rfc-6902
+type: task
+title: "Review applyPatch conformance to RFC 6902"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+Request: users report applyPatch accepting patches they consider invalid, unexpected edge-case results and
+unexpected failure behaviour; make it conform to RFC 6902 in every case, errors included.
+
+Review (RFC 6902 sections 3, 4.1-4.6, 5; pointers per RFC 6901): every operation, the proper-prefix rule
+for move, post-removal index evaluation, `-` handling, deep equality, atomicity and aliasing were checked
+against the implementation with probes. No deviation from the RFC was found in `src/index.ts`, so no code
+change was made; regression tests for the edge cases checked were added to `test/patch.test.ts`.
+Open point: removing the root throws (documented in the README); the RFC does not say what the result
+would be, so this is kept.
diff --git a/test/patch.test.ts b/test/patch.test.ts
index b48e10a7eca9d6c89c34fbb1525b026199c31352..93bc2825098ec5ea5cc284fca851396e2fef2447 100644
--- a/test/patch.test.ts
+++ b/test/patch.test.ts
@@ -177,3 +177,22 @@ test("no prototype pollution; only own members", () => {
   assert.throws(() => ap({}, [{ op: "add", path: "/constructor/prototype/x", value: 1 }]));
   assert.equal(({} as any).x, undefined);
 });
+
+// RFC 6902 sections 4.4 and 4.6: edge cases checked during the conformance review
+test("move: index is evaluated after removal; '-' appends; proper-prefix rule", () => {
+  assert.deepEqual(ap([1, 2, 3], [{ op: "move", from: "/0", path: "/-" }]), [2, 3, 1]);
+  assert.throws(() => ap([1, 2, 3], [{ op: "move", from: "/0", path: "/3" }]));
+  assert.throws(() => ap({ a: { b: 1 } }, [{ op: "move", from: "/a", path: "/a/b/c" }]));
+  assert.throws(() => ap({ a: 1 }, [{ op: "move", from: "/missing", path: "/missing" }]));
+});
+
+test("test: numbers by value, strings are not numbers, empty array is not empty object", () => {
+  assert.doesNotThrow(() => ap({ a: 1 }, [{ op: "test", path: "/a", value: 1.0 }]));
+  assert.throws(() => ap({ a: 1 }, [{ op: "test", path: "/a", value: "1" }]));
+  assert.throws(() => ap({ a: [] }, [{ op: "test", path: "/a", value: {} }]));
+});
+
+test("operation names are case-sensitive; extra members are ignored", () => {
+  assert.throws(() => ap({}, [{ op: "ADD", path: "/a", value: 1 }]));
+  assert.deepEqual(ap({ a: 1 }, [{ op: "copy", from: "/a", path: "/b", value: 5 }]), { a: 1, b: 1 });
+});
